<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean corn imports from U.S. seen plunging.</title>
<headline>S.Korean corn imports from U.S. seen plunging.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. corn exports to South Korea are forecast to fall by 2.6 million tonnes in the current 1996 marketing year (October/September) due to fierce competition from China and Argentina, the U.S. embassy said on Friday.</p>
<p>The U.S. agricultural attache predicted in a report that South Korea's corn imports would total 9.4 million tonnes in 1996. In the 1995 marketing year the U.S. sold 8.6 million tonnes of corn to South Korea and had a 95 percent market share.</p>
<p>U.S. Embassy Seoul Forecast S.Korea Corn Imports 1996 (Oct/Sept)</p>
<p>United States: 6.0 million tonnes</p>
<p>China:	   2.0 million tonnes</p>
<p>Argentina	1.4 million tonnes</p>
<p>TOTAL	    9.4 million tonnes*</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>Processing:    1.8 million tonnes (1.6 million tonnes U.S. origin)</p>
<p>Feed	     7.6 million tonnes</p>
<p>* Estimated purchases to date include U.S. 3.7 million tonnes, China 1.2 million tonnes, Argentina 300,000 tonnes (Expected to deliver another 1.1 million tonnes May/June). The balance of 1.4 million tonnes expected to be split between U.S. and China.</p>
</text>
